** ======================================================================
** Stage 1: tail alone in CalculiX, without water.
** Quasi-static pressure ramp in chamber L (0 -> P_MAX).
** ======================================================================
** Mesh, node sets and material are generated by tools/make_geometry.py solid .
*INCLUDE, INPUT=tail.msh
*INCLUDE, INPUT=tail_sets.nam
*INCLUDE, INPUT=material.inc
**
** Linear ramp in the "time" of the static step (time = load parameter 0..1)
*AMPLITUDE, NAME=RAMP
0., 0., 1., 1.
**
** NLGEOM: geometric nonlinearity – deflections are large (over 10% of the length),
** so linear small-displacement theory would give a wrong shape.
*STEP, NLGEOM, INC=1000
** initial increment 0.05, time 1, min 1e-5, max 0.05 -> at least 20 points
*STATIC, SOLVER=PARDISO
0.05, 1.0, 1e-5, 0.05
**
** Root glued to the rigid head: fully clamped.
*BOUNDARY
Nfix, 1, 3
** 2D model: z is fixed at all nodes (plane strain).
*BOUNDARY
Nall, 3, 3
**
** Pressure on the walls of all cells of chamber L.
** P_MAX = 20 kPa  PLACEHOLDER – to be identified from measurements
** (above ~21 kPa the solution loses convergence, see NOTES.md)
*DLOAD, AMPLITUDE=RAMP
SchL, P, 20000.
**
** Displacement of the tip centre at every increment -> .dat file
*NODE PRINT, NSET=Ntip
U
*NODE FILE
U
*EL FILE
S, E
*END STEP
